{
  "id": "ep010",
  "duration": 61.903,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 5.506,
      "text": "In 1957, astronomers logged a tiny faint star that wasn't a star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "TON 618 SDSS9 version 2.jpg",
        "credit": "Sloan Digital Sky Survey, Apache Point Observatory, Astrophysical Research Consortium",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TON_618_SDSS9_version_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.506,
      "end": 14.526,
      "text": "Braulio Iriarte and Enrique Chavira recorded entry 618 at Mexico's Tonantzintla Observatory as a white dwarf.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Glittering Gathering of Stars in Pismis 26 (52515088826).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glittering_Gathering_of_Stars_in_Pismis_26_(52515088826).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.5,
          "end": 11.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.333,
          "end": 14.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.526,
      "end": 24.251,
      "text": "In 1970, radio signals from Bologna and spectra from McDonald Observatory revealed entry 618 was a quasar.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "McDonald Observatory 107-inch telescope.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:McDonald_Observatory_107-inch_telescope.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.533,
          "end": 24.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.251,
      "end": 31.946,
      "text": "Its central beacon shines with the brilliance of 140 trillion Suns, drowning out its host galaxy entirely.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of quasar J0313-1806.jpg",
        "credit": "NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/J. da Silva",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_quasar_J0313-1806.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.267,
          "end": 27.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.767,
          "end": 31.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.946,
      "end": 41.766,
      "text": "Infalling gas whirls around the core at speeds up to 10,500 kilometers per second, lighting up a nebula three times wider than the Milky Way.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "2'Coming of Age' in Cosmic Blobs.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2%27Coming_of_Age%27_in_Cosmic_Blobs.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.933,
          "end": 35.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 35.433,
          "end": 41.767,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.766,
      "end": 52.641,
      "text": "Depending on the spectral line analyzed, astronomers estimate its central black hole contains between 40.7 and 66 billion solar masses.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Anatomy of a Black Hole.jpg",
        "credit": "European Southern Observatory - ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatomy_of_a_Black_Hole.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.767,
          "end": 48.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 48.133,
          "end": 52.633,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 52.641,
      "end": 61.553,
      "text": "Light from this ultramassive engine traveled 10.8 billion years to reach Earth, where entry 618 looked like a tiny faint star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "TON 618 SDSS9 version 2.jpg",
        "credit": "Sloan Digital Sky Survey, Apache Point Observatory, Astrophysical Research Consortium",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TON_618_SDSS9_version_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 52.633,
          "end": 61.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
